Dear all,

please find attached the quality alert QA-26-017 regarding the TIB men's down=
 vest (style J10911A00305, all colours).

We have received a few reports from boutiques about the zipper slider detachi=
ng from the chain or not closing
properly after some days of wear. The issue is linked to a supplier batch of =
sliders and concerns units delivered to
stores from 1 September 2026. Return rate on the affected units is currently =
below 3%, so there is no reason to
remove the style from the floor.

What we need from you, starting today:
1. Accept the return or exchange of affected TIB vests, also without receipt =
if the client is in the CRM.
2. Use return reason DEF in the POS (not QUALITY, not CHANGE_MIND).
3. Do NOT repair in store. Put the piece in the quarantine box with the attac=
hed form filled in.
4. Every Friday ship the quarantine box back to your DC (CSG for EMEA, TKO fo=
r APAC, NJ for Americas) with the
   return label "QA-26-017".
5. Check the TIB on the floor: if the slider is loose, take the piece off sal=
e and treat it as point 3.

Please do not communicate anything to clients beyond "we will exchange it imm=
ediately". No posts, no comments on
social media. Press questions go to Corporate Communications.

Thank you for your cooperation,
Elena Rinaldi
Product Quality & After-Sales

